<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    ArtMoon main screen — the STAGE. Ported from app/gui/, not designed here.

    Nik's rule (2026-10-12): "If its user facing it needs to look like every other platform,
    meaning we port over what we already have, we dont reinvent the wheel."

    Structure, from the QML and nothing else:
      HomeScreen.qml:1975  HostStage fills below the tab strip — top _px(14), sides _px(44),
                           bottom _px(18).
      HostStage.qml:555    the card is `width: stage._cardW`, and HostStage.qml:280 defines
                           _cardW = round(width * 0.55). It is the LEFT 55%, not a full-bleed
                           card. The right 45% is GameFacts (_px(58) action buttons under it).
      HostStage.qml:863    nameBlock — top _px(20), left _px(38); name at 68 Bold, tracking
                           -2.4*u; sub-line at Theme.fontTitle (19).
      HostStage.qml:1121   fieldRow — top _px(32) below the identity block, spacing _px(32).

    EVERY dimension in this file is the QML's BASE number, unscaled — 44, 14, 18, 38, 20, 68,
    19, 32. AmScale.applyTo() multiplies them by Theme.uiScale (width / 1330) at bind time,
    which is the desktop's own _px(). Do not tidy these into tuned dp: a literal that happens
    to match by luck is drift the moment the window changes width.

    Gone from the old card, because the desktop does not have them: the 56sp fixed title, the
    second HOST LINK block, and the full-bleed hero background.
-->
<!--
    ⚠️ THE STAGE'S INSETS ARE NOT HERE. They live on the GridView (pc_grid_view.xml: padding
    44 / 14 / 44 / 18), because this item's height is set to the GridView's own height at bind
    time (PcGridAdapter.getView). Margins on the ITEM add to that height instead of coming off
    it: 14 + 18 of them made the grid's content 32dp taller than its viewport, which is why the
    page scrolled a little when it should not scroll at all — and why the bottom of the card,
    where the action row sits, was the part below the fold. Insets belong to the box that holds
    the list, not to the rows inside it.
-->
<FrameLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:id="@+id/am_hero_root"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent">

    <LinearLayout
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="match_parent"
        android:orientation="horizontal">

        <!-- ══════ the card — 55%, radius 16, backdrop inside ══════ -->
        <FrameLayout
            android:id="@+id/am_stage_card"
            android:layout_width="0dp"
            android:layout_height="match_parent"
            android:layout_weight="0.55"
            android:background="@drawable/am_stage_card"
            android:clipToOutline="true">

            <ImageView
                android:id="@+id/am_hero_bg_image"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:scaleType="centerCrop"
                android:visibility="gone"
                android:contentDescription="@null" />

            <!-- The backdrop ramp. Its stops are a function of the host's colour pair
                 (HostStage.qml:113-185), so it is a Drawable built in code — AmBackdropRamp —
                 not a shape in here. It runs along X: flat for the first 55% of the card at
                 what the composite produced, then falling away to #05080a, so the identity
                 block has something to sit on and the right of the card still reads as a
                 colour. The VERTICAL scrim this replaced darkened the strip the action row
                 lives in and left the left of the card lighter than the desktop. -->
            <View
                android:id="@+id/am_stage_ramp"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="match_parent" />

            <!-- ⚠️ THE BOTTOM MARGIN IS THE ACTION ROW'S OWN HEIGHT, and it is what stops the
                 controls from being the thing that gets cut. It reserves the row's strip at the
                 card's foot so this column measures to the line the row sits on — the same
                 relationship the desktop states at HostStage.qml:1237
                 (`y: Math.min(_idealY, actionRow.y - height - stage._px(20))`, "gives up the gap
                 before it gives up the buttons"). The column clips what does not fit, so a short
                 card costs the tail of the block above rather than the buttons. Both numbers go
                 through AmScale, so they stay one number at every width. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_marginBottom="58dp"
                android:orientation="vertical"
                android:paddingStart="50dp"
                android:paddingLeft="50dp"
                android:paddingEnd="50dp"
                android:paddingRight="50dp"
                android:paddingTop="20dp"
                android:paddingBottom="0dp"
                android:clipChildren="true">

                <LinearLayout
                    android:id="@+id/am_badge_row"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:orientation="horizontal"
                    android:gravity="center_vertical">

                    <LinearLayout
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="30dp"
                        android:orientation="horizontal"
                        android:gravity="center_vertical"
                        android:background="@drawable/am_hero_badge"
                        android:paddingStart="13dp"
                        android:paddingEnd="13dp">

                        <View
                            android:id="@+id/status_dot"
                            android:layout_width="8dp"
                            android:layout_height="8dp"
                            android:background="@drawable/am_dot_pairing"
                            android:layout_marginEnd="7dp" />

                        <TextView
                            android:id="@+id/status_label"
                            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:textSize="16sp"
                            android:textStyle="bold"
                            android:letterSpacing="0.07"
                            android:textAllCaps="true"
                            android:textColor="@color/am_text2"
                            android:maxLines="1" />
                    </LinearLayout>

                    <LinearLayout
                        android:id="@+id/am_auth_chip"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="30dp"
                        android:layout_marginStart="9dp"
                        android:orientation="horizontal"
                        android:gravity="center_vertical"
                        android:background="@drawable/am_hero_badge"
                        android:paddingStart="13dp"
                        android:paddingEnd="13dp"
                        android:visibility="gone">

                        <View
                            android:layout_width="8dp"
                            android:layout_height="8dp"
                            android:background="@drawable/am_dot_auth"
                            android:layout_marginEnd="7dp" />

                        <TextView
                            android:id="@+id/am_auth_label"
                            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:text="@string/am_hero_auth"
                            android:textSize="16sp"
                            android:textStyle="bold"
                            android:letterSpacing="0.07"
                            android:textAllCaps="true"
                            android:textColor="@color/am_text2"
                            android:maxLines="1" />
                    </LinearLayout>
                </LinearLayout>

                <!-- HostStage.qml:896 — the host name, 68 Bold, tracking -2.4u -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/grid_text"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="20dp"
                    android:textSize="68sp"
                    android:textStyle="bold"
                    android:letterSpacing="-0.035"
                    android:textColor="@color/am_text"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:ellipsize="end" />

                <!-- HostStage.qml:1038-1103 — the status line and the stream badges are ONE
                     row, not two. The status text and the badges (resolution, fps, bitrate,
                     HDR, codec, audio) sit on the same line, every child in the same _px(28)
                     box, and when the row cannot fit it shrinks as a whole rather than
                     wrapping — see PcGridAdapter.bindSublRow().

                     The desktop tried a second line first and turned it down in as many words:
                     "this is one statement, and it reads as one only on one line." -->
                <LinearLayout
                    android:id="@+id/am_subl_row"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="28dp"
                    android:layout_marginTop="8dp"
                    android:orientation="horizontal"
                    android:gravity="center_vertical">

                    <!-- _subLine at Theme.fontTitle (19), vertical centre in the row's box -->
                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/am_ready_line"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:textSize="19sp"
                        android:textColor="@color/am_text2"
                        android:singleLine="true"
                        android:ellipsize="end" />

                    <!-- The desktop's order, and HDR only when the host's settings ask for it
                         (HostStage.qml:1069-1075). -->
                    <TextView android:id="@+id/am_spec_res" style="@style/AmSpecChip"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content" android:layout_height="28dp" />
                    <TextView android:id="@+id/am_spec_fps" style="@style/AmSpecChip"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content" android:layout_height="28dp" />
                    <TextView android:id="@+id/am_spec_bitrate" style="@style/AmSpecChip"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content" android:layout_height="28dp" />
                    <TextView android:id="@+id/am_spec_hdr" style="@style/AmSpecChip"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content" android:layout_height="28dp"
                        android:visibility="gone" />
                    <TextView android:id="@+id/am_spec_codec" style="@style/AmSpecChip"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content" android:layout_height="28dp" />
                    <TextView android:id="@+id/am_spec_audio" style="@style/AmSpecChip"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content" android:layout_height="28dp" />
                </LinearLayout>

                <!-- HostStage.qml:1121 — fieldRow, _px(32) below the identity block -->
                <LinearLayout
                    android:id="@+id/am_hostlink_block"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="32dp"
                    android:orientation="vertical"
                    android:visibility="gone">

                    <TextView
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:text="@string/am_host_link"
                        android:textSize="13sp"
                        android:textStyle="bold"
                        android:letterSpacing="0.09"
                        android:textAllCaps="true"
                        android:textColor="@color/am_text3" />

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/am_hostlink_value"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:textSize="28sp"
                        android:textStyle="bold"
                        android:textColor="@color/am_text" />
                </LinearLayout>

            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/am_last_session"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="28dp"
                android:orientation="vertical"
                android:visibility="gone">

                <!-- HostStage.qml:1259-1294 — WHEN, as a bordered badge: height _px(30),
                     radius _px(6), no fill, 1px Theme.line. "LAST SESSION" at _px(15) DemiBold in
                     _onBg2, the age uppercased beside it at the same size in _onBg3, _px(9) apart,
                     _px(13) of padding either side.

                     It used to be bare text with no box that never said WHEN — the age was folded
                     into the same string as the duration. -->
                <LinearLayout
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="30dp"
                    android:orientation="horizontal"
                    android:gravity="center_vertical"
                    android:background="@drawable/am_facts_badge"
                    android:paddingStart="13dp"
                    android:paddingLeft="13dp"
                    android:paddingEnd="13dp"
                    android:paddingRight="13dp">

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/am_last_session_when"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:text="@string/am_last_session"
                        android:textSize="15sp"
                        android:textStyle="bold"
                        android:letterSpacing="0.073"
                        android:textAllCaps="true"
                        android:textColor="@color/am_text2" />

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/am_last_session_ago"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_marginStart="9dp"
                        android:layout_marginLeft="9dp"
                        android:textSize="15sp"
                        android:textStyle="bold"
                        android:letterSpacing="0.073"
                        android:textAllCaps="true"
                        android:textColor="@color/am_text3" />
                </LinearLayout>

                <!-- HostStage.qml:1299-1337 — grade and duration on one line. The grade KEEPS its
                     tinted pill (height _px(42), radius _px(8), its colour at 16% alpha, text
                     _px(21) in that colour); the duration does not — "a bordered box around a
                     plain fact was a second frame this panel did not need". -->
                <LinearLayout
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="18dp"
                    android:orientation="horizontal"
                    android:gravity="center_vertical">

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/am_last_session_grade"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="42dp"
                        android:gravity="center"
                        android:textSize="21sp"
                        android:textStyle="bold"
                        android:paddingStart="15dp"
                        android:paddingLeft="15dp"
                        android:paddingEnd="15dp"
                        android:paddingRight="15dp"
                        android:visibility="gone" />

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/am_last_session_duration"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_marginStart="10dp"
                        android:layout_marginLeft="10dp"
                        android:textSize="21sp"
                        android:textColor="@color/am_text2" />
                </LinearLayout>

                <!-- HostStage.qml:1340-1392 — the three headline numbers. Each is a value at
                     _px(46) DemiBold with its UNIT beside it at _px(18) on the same baseline,
                     over an uppercased caption at _px(14). _px(34) apart.

                     ⚠️ The unit is a separate view and the value is a bare number. It used to be
                     one string ("12 ms"), which cannot baseline-align against the number and
                     cannot hide the unit when the host never measured the figure. -->
                <LinearLayout
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="18dp"
                    android:orientation="horizontal">

                    <LinearLayout
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_marginEnd="34dp"
                        android:layout_marginRight="34dp"
                        android:orientation="vertical">

                        <LinearLayout
                            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:orientation="horizontal">

                            <TextView android:id="@+id/am_last_session_rtt"
                                android:layout_width="wrap_content" android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                android:textSize="46sp" android:textStyle="bold"
                                android:textColor="@color/am_text" />

                            <TextView android:id="@+id/am_last_session_rtt_unit"
                                android:layout_width="wrap_content" android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                android:layout_marginBottom="7dp" android:layout_gravity="bottom"
                                android:textSize="18sp" android:textColor="@color/am_text3" />
                        </LinearLayout>

                        <TextView android:id="@+id/am_last_session_rtt_caption"
                            android:layout_width="wrap_content" android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:text="@string/am_stat_rtt" android:textSize="14sp"
                            android:textStyle="bold" android:letterSpacing="0.114"
                            android:textAllCaps="true" android:textColor="@color/am_text3" />
                    </LinearLayout>

                    <LinearLayout
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_marginEnd="34dp"
                        android:layout_marginRight="34dp"
                        android:orientation="vertical">

                        <LinearLayout
                            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:orientation="horizontal">

                            <TextView android:id="@+id/am_last_session_hostlat"
                                android:layout_width="wrap_content" android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                android:textSize="46sp" android:textStyle="bold"
                                android:textColor="@color/am_text" />

                            <TextView android:id="@+id/am_last_session_hostlat_unit"
                                android:layout_width="wrap_content" android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                android:layout_marginBottom="7dp" android:layout_gravity="bottom"
                                android:textSize="18sp" android:textColor="@color/am_text3" />
                        </LinearLayout>

                        <TextView
                            android:layout_width="wrap_content" android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:text="@string/am_stat_hostlat" android:textSize="14sp"
                            android:textStyle="bold" android:letterSpacing="0.114"
                            android:textAllCaps="true" android:textColor="@color/am_text3" />
                    </LinearLayout>

                    <LinearLayout
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:orientation="vertical">

                        <LinearLayout
                            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:orientation="horizontal">

                            <TextView android:id="@+id/am_last_session_drops"
                                android:layout_width="wrap_content" android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                android:textSize="46sp" android:textStyle="bold"
                                android:textColor="@color/am_text" />

                            <TextView android:id="@+id/am_last_session_drops_unit"
                                android:layout_width="wrap_content" android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                                android:layout_marginBottom="7dp" android:layout_gravity="bottom"
                                android:textSize="18sp" android:textColor="@color/am_text3" />
                        </LinearLayout>

                        <TextView
                            android:layout_width="wrap_content" android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:text="@string/am_stat_drops" android:textSize="14sp"
                            android:textStyle="bold" android:letterSpacing="0.114"
                            android:textAllCaps="true" android:textColor="@color/am_text3" />
                    </LinearLayout>
                </LinearLayout>

                <!-- HostStage.qml:1214 — "No cover strip. The credited-games artwork it used to
                     carry was sized for the old right-hand column, and the numbers are the part
                     worth reading from the card." The 48x72 tile strip that stood here is gone
                     because the desktop deleted it, not because it was in the way. -->
            </LinearLayout>
                <View
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="0dp"
                    android:layout_weight="1" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <!-- HostStage.qml:1424-1477 — the action row at the card's foot. One row of
                     controls on ONE baseline; the panel pair under the cover and the title
                     (am_panel_action_stack, right column) sits on this same line, so the card
                     has one row of controls that spans both halves rather than two rows at two
                     heights.

                     height _px(58) · radius _px(10) · width = content + _px(54) · _px(12)
                     between buttons. ⚠️ radius _px(10), NOT a full-round pill: 10 is the
                     desktop's number and a 28dp radius on a 58dp-tall button is what drew the
                     two end caps through each other.

                     ⚠️ THE BACKGROUND IS NOT HERE. A button is #14ffffff with a 1px
                     Theme.lineHigh border when nothing is lit, and its own colour only while
                     focused or hovered (1471-1477). Both are built in code because the radius
                     has to come down with the button: a shape inside a ripple/selector is not a
                     GradientDrawable, so AmScale cannot reach its corners, and those fixed
                     28dp corners were the sliced pill. -->
            <!-- ⚠️ A SIBLING OF THE COLUMN, PINNED TO THE CARD'S FOOT — NOT THE COLUMN'S LAST CHILD.
                 This is a fix, not a tidy-up. As the last child it was the thing that fell off
                 the card when the card ran out of height: on the Fold's cover screen the card is
                 279dp while its contents want ~292dp, so Open and Options were drawn with their
                 bottoms past the card's edge and Nik saw "just the very top of the button".
                 Measured on the device at 1972x1248 / 420dpi: the row was given 52px of its 86px.

                 The desktop settled the direction at HostStage.qml:1237 — the buttons are the
                 fixed datum and the block above them gives way ("gives up the gap before it gives
                 up the buttons"). This is that rule: the column above is measured to the row's own
                 line, and this row is always whole.

                 The desktop's numbers for this row are HostStage.qml:1428-1429 —
                 `anchors.leftMargin: stage._px(38)`, `anchors.bottomMargin: stage._px(30)` — and
                 this port deviates from BOTH, deliberately, each one seen and approved on Nik's
                 own screen. Do not "restore" either without asking him.

                   - 50dp, not 38: the card's content sat "right on the left edge of the image"
                     while the desktop sat "a bit more to the right". The desktop's 38 is a fixed
                     fraction of its 1330px stage; on a phone the window is ~751dp, so the same 38
                     lands at 0.565x = 21.5dp — the same proportion of the card, but 5.6mm in the
                     hand against ~1.7cm on a monitor, which reads as no inset at all. 50dp puts
                     it at ~9% of the card. The column's paddingStart/paddingEnd carry the same
                     number so the buttons and the text stay on one line.
                   - 15dp, not 30: "You moved them slightly to high now, moved them down half of
                     what you moved them up." At 30 the buttons floated; at 0 they were the thing
                     that clipped. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/am_action_row"
                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_gravity="bottom"
                android:layout_marginStart="50dp"
                android:layout_marginLeft="50dp"
                android:layout_marginBottom="15dp"
                android:orientation="horizontal">

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/am_action_open"
                        android:focusable="true"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="58dp"
                        android:gravity="center"
                        android:text="@string/am_action_open"
                        android:textSize="19sp"
                        android:textColor="@color/am_text"
                        android:paddingStart="27dp"
                        android:paddingEnd="27dp"
                        android:layout_marginEnd="12dp" />

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/am_action_options"
                        android:focusable="true"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="58dp"
                        android:gravity="center"
                        android:text="@string/am_action_options"
                        android:textSize="19sp"
                        android:textColor="@color/am_text"
                        android:paddingStart="27dp"
                        android:paddingEnd="27dp" />
            </LinearLayout>
        </FrameLayout>

        <!-- ══════ the right 45% — GameFacts / LAST SESSION ══════ -->
        <FrameLayout
            android:id="@+id/am_stage_panel"
            android:layout_width="0dp"
            android:layout_height="match_parent"
            android:layout_weight="0.45">

        <!-- ══════ the right column — GameFacts (app/gui/GameFacts.qml) ══════

             What the desktop puts beside the card (HostStage.qml:1625-1694, `lastPanel`).

             ⚠️ IT IS THREE THINGS — badge, cover, title — AND NOTHING ELSE. The desktop says so
             at the call site, in as many words:

                 store: ""   metaExtra: ""   played: ""   sessions: 0
                 "Deliberately all empty: title and cover, nothing else. The hours are in the
                  badge above the picture and the age beside them, so repeating them under the
                  title would be saying them twice."

             So there is no meta row here and no figure row: with `played` empty and `sessions`
             0, GameFacts' own `visible:` conditions hide both (GameFacts.qml:317 and 385). A
             PLAYED figure fed from the host's session length was this port inventing a second
             place to state the duration the card already shows, in the one number the desktop
             deliberately keeps out of this block.

             Geometry, every number BASE and scaled by AmScale:
               165  column spacing _px(18)
               168  badge _px(30) tall, radius _px(6), width = content + _px(26), no fill
               180  badge text Theme.fontBody (16) DemiBold, uppercased, tracking 1.1u
               224  cover radius _px(10); height from availableHeight at bind time
               249  title at Theme.fontDisplay (34) Bold, tracking -0.7u

             ⚠️ THE COLUMN AND THE COVER BOTH START GONE. An empty map means draw nothing at all
             — "There is no empty state — the card simply goes back to what it looks like without
             one" (HostStage.qml:1611-1613). Both were VISIBLE on first inflation, which is what
             put a filled, outlined rectangle the size of a cover on the right of the screen
             before any host had said anything: a picture-shaped hole that is not a picture. -->

        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/am_facts_col"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_gravity="top"
            android:layout_marginTop="30dp"
            android:paddingEnd="46dp"
            android:paddingRight="46dp"
            android:orientation="vertical"
            android:gravity="center_horizontal"
            android:visibility="gone">

            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/am_facts_badge"
                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                android:layout_height="30dp"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:background="@drawable/am_facts_badge"
                android:paddingStart="13dp"
                android:paddingLeft="13dp"
                android:paddingEnd="13dp"
                android:paddingRight="13dp"
                android:visibility="gone">

                <!-- HostStage.qml:1666 — badgeDot: Theme.accent while a session is running,
                     and nothing at all when one is not ("transparent"). It pulses on the
                     900ms rhythm of the host page's STREAMING tag (AppsScreen.qml:1655-1665);
                     the pulse is PcGridAdapter.paintLiveDot's, and it holds still when the
                     system asks animations off. -->
                <View
                    android:id="@+id/am_facts_badge_dot"
                    android:layout_width="8dp"
                    android:layout_height="8dp"
                    android:layout_gravity="center_vertical"
                    android:layout_marginEnd="9dp"
                    android:layout_marginRight="9dp"
                    android:background="@drawable/am_dot_live"
                    android:visibility="gone" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/am_facts_badge_main"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:textSize="16sp"
                    android:textStyle="bold"
                    android:letterSpacing="0.069"
                    android:textAllCaps="true"
                    android:textColor="@color/am_text2" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/am_facts_badge_muted"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginStart="9dp"
                    android:layout_marginLeft="9dp"
                    android:textSize="16sp"
                    android:textStyle="bold"
                    android:letterSpacing="0.069"
                    android:textAllCaps="true"
                    android:textColor="@color/am_text3" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <!-- GameFacts puts the picture at 2:3 and lets nothing stretch it: the cover's
                 HEIGHT decides its width (GameFacts.qml:150-156, `implicitWidth` off the art and
                 `byWidth = width * 3 / 2` as the cap), which is why the panel is _px(380) wide
                 and the art is narrower than that. So the width is set from the height at bind
                 time and the image is centred, not matched to the column. -->
            <ImageView
                android:id="@+id/am_facts_cover"
                android:layout_width="180dp"
                android:layout_height="180dp"
                android:layout_gravity="center_horizontal"
                android:layout_marginTop="18dp"
                android:scaleType="centerCrop"
                android:background="@drawable/am_facts_cover_frame"
                android:clipToOutline="true"
                android:visibility="gone"
                android:contentDescription="@null" />

            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/am_facts_title"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="18dp"
                android:gravity="center"
                android:textSize="34sp"
                android:textStyle="bold"
                android:letterSpacing="-0.021"
                android:maxLines="3"
                android:ellipsize="end"
                android:textColor="@color/am_text" />
        </LinearLayout>

        <!-- ══════ before the first game — HostStage.qml:1898-1957 ══════

             Nothing has been played here yet, so there is no block to draw — but there is still
             something to SAY, and hiding the column entirely was wrong. The desktop's own words:

               "The badge the block will carry, and one line — centred in the space where the block
                will stand, level with the middle of the card. It sat on the line where Play again
                will appear at first, and read as a footnote down there (Marcello, 18/09/2026)."

             ⚠️ Deliberately NOT an outline of the block. The desktop built that first — the
             cover's exact box, dashed, with "Your last game" at title size — and calls it "the
             ugliest thing on the screen: the largest object on that side, holding nothing, so the
             eye went to it and found a hole." Anything that draws the shape of the missing cover
             repeats that mistake.

             The badge is GameFacts' own recipe (@drawable/am_facts_badge — height _px(30),
             radius _px(6), no fill, 1px Theme.line), "so it is the same badge the real block will
             show in this place"; its type is Theme.text3 where the real badge's is text2. -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/am_facts_hint"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_gravity="center_vertical"
            android:paddingEnd="46dp"
            android:paddingRight="46dp"
            android:orientation="vertical"
            android:gravity="center_horizontal"
            android:visibility="gone">

            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/am_facts_hint_badge"
                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                android:layout_height="30dp"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:background="@drawable/am_facts_badge"
                android:paddingStart="13dp"
                android:paddingLeft="13dp"
                android:paddingEnd="13dp"
                android:paddingRight="13dp">

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/am_facts_hint_badge_text"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:textSize="16sp"
                    android:textStyle="bold"
                    android:letterSpacing="0.069"
                    android:textAllCaps="true"
                    android:textColor="@color/am_text3" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <!-- _px(12) below the badge, and it wraps inside the panel's width rather than
                 running off the edge (the desktop caps it at lastPanel.width). -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/am_facts_hint_text"
                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="12dp"
                android:gravity="center_horizontal"
                android:textSize="16sp"
                android:textColor="@color/am_text2" />
        </LinearLayout>


            <!-- ══════ the panel pair — HostStage.qml:1694-1896 ══════

                 Resume/Play again, and Stop BESIDE it while something is streaming. This is the
                 half Nik could not find: it is NOT in the action row, and that is the point of
                 the arrangement — "down there it read as a generic verb next to Open and
                 Profiles, with the game it refers to a card's width away. Under the cover and
                 the title, 'Play again' has already been told what it plays."

                 Same body, same height _px(58) and same radius _px(10) as the action row, and
                 anchored so its BOTTOM sits on that row's line: the card has one row of
                 controls that happens to span both halves rather than two rows at two heights.

                 It grew UPWARD until 12 October 2026 and now grows SIDEWAYS: Resume, then Stop
                 to its right. Downward was never available — it would draw it over the footer
                 prompts — and sideways costs the floor nothing. It also puts the pair in the
                 order the pad already walks them (Resume is the stop past the action row, Stop
                 the stop after that), so left and right now move the way the eye reads them.
                 The desktop's lastPanel measures its available height from the top of this
                 stack, so with one row instead of two the block above gains the 68px it used
                 to give up rather than the button leaving the card.

                 ⚠️ ITS HORIZONTAL CENTRE IS THE PICTURE'S CENTRE, and that is what the two
                 insets below are for. The desktop puts the pair on the block's own axis —
                 HostStage.qml:1866, `anchors.horizontalCenter: lastPanel.horizontalCenter` —
                 and the block is inset from the right edge by _px(46). Centring this stack in
                 the PANEL instead (which is what `layout_gravity="bottom|center_horizontal"`
                 and a wrap_content width did) puts it half of that inset — 23dp — to the right
                 of the cover and the title above it. Nik, 12 October, with it boxed on the
                 Fold: "its not centered its off to one side, it should be centered in relation
                 to the image". match_parent + the same 46dp end inset gives this stack the
                 SAME content box the column has, so the two axes are the same axis by
                 construction rather than by a number that has to be kept in step. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/am_panel_action_stack"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_gravity="bottom"
                android:layout_marginBottom="30dp"
                android:paddingEnd="46dp"
                android:paddingRight="46dp"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:baselineAligned="false"
                android:gravity="center_horizontal"
                android:visibility="gone">

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/am_panel_resume"
                    android:focusable="true"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="58dp"
                    android:gravity="center"
                    android:text="@string/am_panel_play_again"
                    android:textSize="19sp"
                    android:textColor="@color/am_text"
                    android:paddingStart="27dp"
                    android:paddingEnd="27dp" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/am_panel_stop"
                    android:focusable="true"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="58dp"
                    android:layout_marginStart="10dp"
                    android:layout_marginLeft="10dp"
                    android:gravity="center"
                    android:text="@string/am_stop"
                    android:textSize="19sp"
                    android:textColor="@color/am_danger"
                    android:paddingStart="27dp"
                    android:paddingEnd="27dp"
                    android:visibility="gone" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <!-- kept so the adapter's existing binding keeps working; the desktop has no
                 glyph well on the stage, so it stays gone unless there is something to say -->
            <FrameLayout
                android:id="@+id/am_glyph_well"
                android:layout_width="40dp"
                android:layout_height="40dp"
                android:layout_gravity="bottom|end"
                android:layout_marginEnd="16dp"
                android:layout_marginBottom="12dp"
                android:alpha="0.55"
                android:visibility="gone">

                <ImageView android:id="@+id/grid_image"
                    android:layout_width="40dp" android:layout_height="40dp"
                    android:scaleType="fitCenter" />

                <ImageView android:id="@+id/grid_overlay"
                    android:layout_width="24dp" android:layout_height="24dp"
                    android:layout_gravity="center" android:scaleType="fitCenter" />

                <ProgressBar android:id="@+id/grid_spinner"
                    android:layout_width="32dp" android:layout_height="32dp"
                    android:layout_gravity="center" android:indeterminate="true"
                    android:visibility="gone" />
            </FrameLayout>
        </FrameLayout>
    </LinearLayout>
</FrameLayout>
